# D-110 (steps/defects.md): a consumer's uses were its body's alone -- P0 hangs a `return:` after the body
# on the frame as its trailer, and the walk (l2_uses_walk_frame) never read it.  `rd`'s one read is its
# `return: m\a`, so its uses were empty and any Structure passed was admitted: `rd(Lacks)` (the type as
# the actual, admitted by uses since slice 1 of implements) translated and read a slot `Lacks` has not.
# Now the walk reads the trailer too (l2_uses_walk_body): refused at the call.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Lacks:
    size_t: b 20U
end: Lacks
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: go () size_t
return: rd(Lacks)

size_t: got 0U
got: go()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
